  "label": "Child Innocence Stereotype",
  "description": "The image uses the visual trope of a child pointing to their eyes to symbolize innocence, purity, or a childlike perspective. This is a common cultural reference that implies the child is speaking with unfiltered honesty or moral clarity. The gesture is often associated with 'I see what you're saying' or 'I believe this' in memes, enhancing the sincerity of the message.",
